<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112741" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῠτάλμιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Lyc.
			341
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύω</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>producing, nourishing,
			fostering,</i> epith. of gods, as of Poseidon, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Clara Rhodos</u>
				6
			</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
				7.386
			</span></i> (Camirus, <span class="entity">iii/ii B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.158e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.5051
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				12(1).905
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Rhodes</span>), etc.; of Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(5).13
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">Ios</span>); of parents, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυτάλμιοι γέροντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					327
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μητρὶ καὶ φ. πατρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					788
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέκτρα φ.</span>
			<i>the marriage</i> bed, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				920
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. χθών</span> Lyc.l.c.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φ.</span>”
				<i>productive power,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.994b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>by birth,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλαῶν ὀμμάτων ἆρα καὶ ἦσθα
				φυτάλμιος;</span> didst thou <i>bring</i> blind eyes with
			thee <i>to life?</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				151
			</span></i> (lyr.). (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυτάλμιος</span> is said
			by <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				803.4
			</span></i>. to be formed by metath. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυτάλιμος,</span> which is prob. coined <i>ad
		hoc.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
